Chapter: ProbeClosureLuck2

 probe-closure-luck faulted before printing anything, including its FIRST
 line -- a line that printed 47 in probe-closure-solo. This drops only
 the third statement to find out whether the fault really belongs to a
 later statement, or whether output was simply lost.

 Output is known to survive a fault: probe-closure-nocapture printed
 `direct-bare 47` and then dumped registers. So if `a` and `b` print
 here, the third statement in probe-closure-luck broke the first one.

Section: Shapes

  add3 : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  add3 (x) (y) (z) = x + y + z

  make-adder : Integer -> (Integer, Integer -> Integer)
  make-adder (n) = add3 n

Section: Driver

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("a 47 expected: " & show (((make-adder 5) 20) 22))
    print-line-uni ("b 6 expected: " & show (((add3 1) 2) 3))
  end
